("""## Q4. What is ‘DataFrame’ in pandas and how is it different from pandas.Series? Explain with an example.

A **DataFrame** in pandas is a two-dimensional labeled data structure that contains rows and columns, similar to an Excel table or SQL table.

A **Series** is a one-dimensional labeled array that can hold data of any type.

### Difference between Series and DataFrame

| Feature | Series | DataFrame |
|---|---|
| Dimension | One-dimensional |
| Structure | Single column |
| Data Representation | Array-like |
| Example | Student marks |

| Feature | DataFrame |
|---|---|
| Dimension | Two-dimensional |
| Structure | Multiple columns |
| Data Representation | Table-like |
| Example | Student database |
""", "markdown"),

